@groovyfoodiess 
https://tasty.co/recipe/refreshing-mango-lassi

Mango lassi is a refreshing and creamy yogurt-based drink that originates from India. Made with ripe mangoes, plain yogurt, and a hint of cardamom, it blends the tanginess of yogurt with the sweetness of mangoes for a delicious summer beverage. If you like it chilled, you can add a few ice cubes before serving.

@groovyfoodiess 

Shakshuka is a North African and Middle Eastern dish of poached eggs in a spiced tomato and pepper sauce. Typically seasoned with cumin, paprika, and garlic, it's often served with crusty bread for dipping. The dish is enjoyed as a hearty breakfast or brunch but can be eaten at any time of the day.

https://tasty.co/recipe/shakshuka

@groovyfoodiess

https://tasty.co/recipe/chocolate-black-sesame-rice-krispies

Chocolate black sesame rice krispies are a delicious and unique twist on the classic rice krispies treat! This version incorporates the nutty, slightly bitter flavor of black sesame seeds with the rich taste of chocolate, adding a mature edge to the traditional marshmallow and rice cereal base.

@groovyfoodiess
This classic BLT sandwich is elevated with crispy oven-baked bacon, juicy seasoned tomatoes, and fresh lettuce, all nestled between buttery, toasted sourdough bread. A tangy and zesty mayo-mustard sauce ties everything together, making each bite irresistible.
 https://tasty.co/recipe/blta-sandwich

@groovyfoodiess 
The ramen omelette cart in Malaysia is a popular street food vendor known for its unique fusion of Japanese and Malaysian flavors. It serves delicious ramen noodles wrapped in a fluffy omelette, creating a savory and satisfying meal that's loved by locals and tourists! The cart often attracts long lines, so instead of waiting in that, come try this delicious twist at home! 
https://tasty.co/recipe/ramen-omelette

@groovyfoodiess

https://tasty.co/recipe/korean-cold-noodles

Korean cold noodles, or naengmyeon, are a refreshing dish featuring long, chewy noodles made from buckwheat or sweet potato starch, served in an icy broth. This dish is typically garnished with slices of cucumber, radish, pear, and protein.

