Hear me out. I have a suggestion to make your life way easier this cookie-making season! Instead of making individual Linzer cookies, bake a sheet tray tart and cut it into little bars to save you time and the hassle of making cookies. These bars feature my tart base recipe paired with a homemade sumac-strawberry jam and sesame sprinkle. WOW! You gotta add this treat to your Christmas cookie box, no doubt!

Full recipe on BenGingi.com

@jasmineandtea 

Here’s a simple yet delicious appetizer for your holiday dinner.
Place prosciutto into phyllo shells, then cover with a generous slice of brie. Top with a dollop of jam, sprinkle with dried thyme leaves, and bake at 350°F for 8-10 minutes. Finish with a few pomegranate seeds on each bite, and enjoy!

@jasmineandtea 

Christmas wreath pretzels  ~ the perfect sweet & salty snack!

Melt white chocolate, then stir in a few drops of green food color. Dip pretzels halfway in the chocolate and arrange them in a circle on parchment paper, layering them twice to make edible wreaths. Add holiday sprinkles and place in the fridge to harden for a fun and tasty holiday treat!

